fect than link himself  we get our first glimpse at who is most  likely impa in the throne room  impa is actually seen twice in this  trailer once in the throne room and once  outside the malus infested hyrule castle  we will probably get to see her side of  the story assisting link and zelda in  the fight against ganon  there are also tiny clues to elemental  imbued weapons as well in certain combat  scenes  erbozo's rocking her signature scimitar  of the seven that is electrified  naturally during combat  and rivali is possibly using some sort  of gale arrows this could just be crazy  enemy knockback due to the nature of  most musou games but the way the enemies  fly in the air and the wind effects  circling the arrows suggest otherwise  there's been speculation that gale  arrows were scrapped idea for breath of  the wild so this is not completely  impossible  towards the end of the trailer link is  finally seen with the signature  champions tunic and master sword  he's seen sword clashing with some sort  of thunder type weapon but on closer  inspection the tip of the blade is  nothing like any current electric breath  of the wild weapon  and as we suspected that is definitely  the highland shield that link has  equipped which has never canonically  been shown in any cut scene as something  link would use in breath of the wild  until now maybe we'll finally see how he  got it and how it ended up in the  basement of hyrule castle  finally we got a tease of what's  possibly an entirely new enemy or friend  in the front cover box art this mini  guardian remains a mystery for now but  is most probably extremely important as  its front and center of the champions  hyrule warriors age of calamity is set  to release november 20th  with more details coming ahead of its  release in september 26th this will more  than likely have more gameplay details  and story as to keep a tight lip on the  plot  even though we all know how it ends for  all things breath of the wild we'll keep  you informed with in-depth  content so stay tuned right here on  [Music]  gamespot  you
 

